lib/src/ - implementation
=========================

    cgra.c       POSIX serial transport, legacy v2/v3 primitives, monotonic
                 transaction budgets, owned diagnostics and explicit plans.
    vector.c     Element-wise kernels, ReLU and MAC dot product.
    kernels.c    Geometry-aware matvec, scan and implicit convolution tiles;
                 convolution has bounded stack workspace, no dense Toeplitz.
    buffers.h    Shared array-footprint and overlap checks.
    bitvec.h     Defined conversions and 16-bit modular arithmetic helpers.
    emu.[ch]     Clockless functional model of the legacy parser and PE mesh,
                 used by sim: and the configurable/stoppable PTY service.
    serve.c      POSIX PTY service; v2/v3 geometries, cancellation descriptor.
    block_wire.* Experimental escaped framing, length checks and header/payload
                 CRC. Private code; no new legacy device capability advertised.
    block_model.* Resident dot/session/dedup functional oracle, exercised by
                 test_blocks. Not yet connected to RTL, public API or CLI;
                 see ../../doc/block-protocol.md and B01-B03 in TASKS.md.

Contracts
---------
- Dependencies: libc and POSIX termios/poll/PTY interfaces. The currently
  verified packaging platform is x86_64 Linux.
- A cgra_t is not locked: serialise calls per handle. Public ownership,
  capacity, aliasing and partial-output rules are in include/cgra.h and
  libcgra(3). Plans copy configuration and require explicit resident binding.
- CFG/WR and EXEC with RESET retry complete NACK replies only, assuming intact
  command bytes and frame lengths. RUN/RD are never retried. Transport failures
  and malformed replies poison the legacy session, invalidate resident plans
  and cached identity, and send no implicit RST. Restore parser alignment
  before reopening; see RECOVERY AND FAULT MODEL in libcgra(3).
- CFG/WR and EXEC input words latch before checksum validation. NACK does not
  roll them back; it prevents EXEC reset/steps. Bulk and bytewise model paths
  reproduce this behavior, checked against production RTL by protocol replay.
- emu.c is one functional reference, not an independent proof of its own
  correctness. Scalar oracles, RTL replay and selected formal RTL properties
  provide distinct checks. The model has no clock/watchdog or UART timing;
  its host execution rate is not FPGA throughput.
- Keep shared legacy constants and row-major 16-bit semantics aligned with
  hw/rtl/cgra_pkg.vhd and include/cgra.h. The experimental block framing has
  a separate versioned contract and does not silently replace v2/v3.
